{:paths ["src"]
 ;; This said "src depends only on kotobase-protocol-core", and then declared
 ;; nothing: `:deps {}`. The sentence was right about WHICH repository and the
 ;; map recorded none of it, so the dependency the prose admitted to was
 ;; undeclared from `e46668a` (10:36 JST, 2026-08-05) onward.
 ;;
 ;; Alone among the six surface repos this one really does stop at core —
 ;; `src/kotobase/protocols/ipfs.cljk` requires, measured 2026-09-06:
 ;;
 ;;   kotobase.protocols.blocks  -> kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocol-core
 ;;   kotobase.protocols.http    -> kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocol-core
 ;;
 ;; The rest of the old comment claimed kotobase was TEST-ONLY. That is true
 ;; of this repo's `src/`, which names no namespace from it, and false about
 ;; the classpath: core's `kotobase.protocols.blocks` requires
 ;; `kotobase.store`, so a deployment that loads this surface and never runs
 ;; a test still needs kotobase present. It arrives through core's own
 ;; deps.edn, which is why it is not repeated here — the `:test` alias below
 ;; keeps it only for the LocalStore oracle the suite uses directly.
 ;;
 ;; Undeclared, core resolved for everyone who already had it next door and
 ;; for nobody else. The nbb line below names it by hand; a sibling checkout
 ;; under `orgs/` supplies it by accident. `kbb -M:test` did neither: it
 ;; failed at load with `Could not locate kotobase/protocols/blocks` and ran
 ;; zero tests — a red suite that reported no test result at all.
 ;;
 ;; The pin is a commit on core's default branch. An unmerged SHA is a
 ;; dependency that disappears when its branch does, and `deps.edn` pins have
 ;; no `verify-west-pins` to catch it (root AGENTS.md).
 :deps {
        io.github.kotoba-lang/test {:local/root "../kotoba.test"}
        io.github.kotoba-lang/kotobase-protocol-core {:local/root "../kotoba.kotobaseProtocolCore"}}
 ;; First-class runtime is nbb/cljs (repo-wide runtime priority):
 ;;   kbb --backend sci --classpath "src:test:../kotobase-protocol-core/src:<kotobase>/src" bin/run_tests.cljk
 :aliases
 {:test {:extra-paths ["test"]}}}
